== Incumbents defeated ==
Due to redistricting, many incumbents are forced to compete against each other in the same district, which will result in a higher than usual number of incumbents being defeated in primaries.

=== In primary elections ===
Thirteen representatives lost renomination: Eight were lost in redistricting battles pitting incumbents against each other, and five incumbents lost nomination to non-incumbent challengers. Additionally, one failed to make the ballot for renomination.

==== Democrats ====
Seven Democrats lost renomination: five in redistricting and two to a non-incumbent challenger.
* {{ushr|Michigan|13|}}: [[Hansen Clarke]] (first elected in 2010): redistricted and defeated August 7, 2012 by fellow incumbent [[Gary Peters (Michigan politician)|Gary Peters]]
* {{ushr|Missouri|1|}}: [[Russ Carnahan]] (first elected in 2004): redistricted and defeated August 7, 2012 by fellow incumbent [[William Lacy Clay, Jr.]]
* {{ushr|New Jersey|9|}}: [[Steve Rothman]] (first elected in 1996): redistricted and defeated June 5, 2012 by fellow incumbent [[Bill Pascrell]]
* {{ushr|Ohio|9|}}: [[Dennis Kucinich]] (first elected in 1996): redistricted and defeated March 6, 2012 by fellow incumbent [[Marcy Kaptur]]
* {{ushr|Pennsylvania|12|}}: [[Jason Altmire]] (first elected in 2006): redistricted and defeated April 24, 2012 by fellow incumbent [[Mark Critz]]<ref name="PADemsLoss">{{cite news | url=http://www.nytimes.com/2012/04/26/us/politics/2-house-democrats-defeated-after-opposing-health-law.html | title=2 House Democrats Defeated After Opposing Health Law | first=Jonathan | last=Weisman | date= April 25, 2012 | accessdate=April 26, 2012 | work=The New York Times}}</ref>
* {{ushr|Pennsylvania|17|}}: [[Tim Holden]] (first elected in 1992): defeated April 24, 2012 by challenger [[Matt Cartwright]]<ref name="PADemsLoss"/>
* {{ushr|Texas|16|}}: [[Silvestre Reyes]] (first elected in 1996): defeated May 29, 2012 by challenger [[Beto O'Rourke]]<ref>http://www.politico.com/news/stories/0512/76848.html</ref>

==== Republicans ====
Six Republicans lost renomination: three in redistricting and three to a non-incumbent challenger.
* {{ushr|Arizona|6|}}: [[Ben Quayle]] (first elected in 2010): redistricted and defeated August 28, 2012 by fellow incumbent [[David Schweikert]]
* {{ushr|Florida|3|}}: [[Cliff Stearns]] (first elected in 1988): defeated August 14, 2012 by challenger [[Ted Yoho]]
* {{ushr|Florida|7|}}: [[Sandy Adams]] (first elected in 2010): redistricted and defeated August 14, 2012 by fellow incumbent [[John Mica]]
* {{ushr|Illinois|16|}}: [[Don Manzullo]] (first elected in 1992): redistricted and defeated March 20, 2012 by fellow incumbent [[Adam Kinzinger]]
* {{ushr|Ohio|2|}}: [[Jean Schmidt]] (first elected in 2005): defeated March 6, 2012 by challenger [[Brad Wenstrup]]
* {{ushr|Oklahoma|1}}: [[John A. Sullivan]] (first elected in 2002): defeated June 26, 2012 by challenger [[Jim Bridenstine]]. 
