== Separate elections ==

Two special elections were scheduled apart from the November elections to fill seats that became vacant earlier.

Two additional special elections scheduled concurrently with the November elections are listed in the [[#November elections|next section, "November elections", below]].
* [[Michigan's 11th congressional district special election, 2012]] will be concurrent with the November elections, to fill the vacant seat of [[Thad McCotter]], (R), who resigned on July 6, 2012. <ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.freep.com/article/20120706/NEWS06/120706063/thad-mccotter-resigns-citing-nightmarish-circumstances |title=Rep. Thaddeus McCotter resigns, citing 'nightmarish' circumstances |date=July 6, 2012 |publisher=[[Detroit Free Press]] |accessdate=August 16, 2012}}</ref> 
* [[New Jersey's 10th congressional district special election, 2012]] will be concurrent with the November elections, to fill the vacant seat of [[Donald M. Payne]] (D), who died.
* [[Washington's 1st congressional district special election, 2012]], will be concurrent with the November elections,<ref>{{cite news| url=http://seattletimes.nwsource.com/html/localnews/2017895230_1stdistrict03.html | work=The Seattle Times | first=Mike | last=Baker | title=Gregoire calls a special election to replace Inslee for a month | date=April 2, 2012}}</ref> to fill the vacant seat of [[Jay Inslee]] (D), who resigned.

